No third-party implementation code is included in this repository seed. The core transports use the Zig standard library plus websocket.zig for WebSocket framing, a MIT-licensed fork of Karl Seguin's library maintained for Zig 0.17 (https://tangled.org/zzstoatzz.io/websocket.zig). The selected revision and package hash are pinned for evaluation; its full licence text is retained in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and must ship with distributions that include it. Optional voice support is not part of the basic package; if it is added, libdave, Opus and any other native component will be documented with their exact revisions, licences and notices. Add required third-party notices and attribution when code or dependencies requiring them are introduced. Discord is a third-party service; Diszig is independent.
